---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="IP / Patents - Solo Ghost"
  description="Solo Ghost intellectual property covering structure-aware approaches to adaptive wireless receiver design."
>
  <section class="ip-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY</p>

      <h1>Eight patent applications. One adaptive wireless receiver program.</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        Solo Ghost's intellectual property program covers structure-aware
        approaches to channel acquisition, channel estimation, equalization,
        adaptive receiver processing and signal detection.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ip-boundary">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">PUBLIC DISCLOSURE</p>
        <h2>Research visibility without exposing confidential strategy.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The portfolio is presented here at a high level to communicate the
          research direction and problem areas addressed by the filings.
        </p>

        <p>
          Detailed implementation choices, unpublished extensions, claim
          strategy and other confidential material are intentionally not
          reproduced on this website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">PATENT PORTFOLIO</p>

      <h2>Original work across the wireless receiver chain.</h2>

      <div class="portfolio">
        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">01</span>
            <span class="status">PROVISIONAL · FILED 28 MAR 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Adaptive CSI Acquisition</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Adaptive Channel State Information Acquisition Based on
            Spatial Structure Stability in Wireless Communication Systems
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates adaptive channel-state-information acquisition that
            uses identifiable spatial structure to vary acquisition density
            across a wireless channel.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Channel Acquisition / CSI</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">02</span>
            <span class="status">PROVISIONAL · FILED 06 APR 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Doppler-Adaptive Channel Estimation</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Doppler-Adaptive Channel Estimation Using Subspace
            Stability and Eigenstructure-Aware Tracking
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates robust channel estimation and tracking for time-varying
            MIMO channels under Doppler-induced evolution.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Mobility / Channel Estimation / Tracking</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">03</span>
            <span class="status">COMPLETE SPECIFICATION · FILED 08 APR 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Structure-Aware Banded Equalization</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Structure-Aware Banded Equalization Based on Delay
            Spread in OFDM Systems
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates low-complexity OFDM equalization by exploiting the
            structured support of the frequency-domain channel induced by
            multipath delay spread.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>OFDM / Equalization / Channel Structure</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">04</span>
            <span class="status">PROVISIONAL · FILED 15 APR 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Interference-Aware Adaptive Receiver</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Interference-Aware Adaptive Receiver for OFDM Systems
            Using Dynamic Blending of Diagonal and Structured Channel Models
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates an interference-aware OFDM receiver that adapts between
            conventional and structured channel representations as
            inter-carrier interference changes.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Adaptive Receiver / OFDM / ICI</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">05</span>
            <span class="status">PROVISIONAL · FILED 01 MAY 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Structure-Aware Adaptive Truncation</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Structure-Aware Adaptive Truncation for Signal
            Detection in Multicarrier Communication Systems
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates adaptive determination of processing support for signal
            detection in multicarrier systems affected by time-varying
            interference.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Signal Detection / Multicarrier / Adaptive Processing</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">06</span>
            <span class="status">COMPLETE SPECIFICATION · FILED 03 OCT 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Receiver Representation Validity</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Receiver Representation Validity Inference Based on
            Predicted Reuse Consequence
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates when a retained receiver representation remains
            suitable for continued use as channel conditions change.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Receiver State / Validity</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">07</span>
            <span class="status">COMPLETE SPECIFICATION · FILED 08 OCT 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Receiver-State Modification</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Uncertainty-Qualified Receiver-State Modification
            Using Transition Robustness Evaluation
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates qualification of a proposed receiver-state change
            under uncertain observations.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Adaptive Receiver / State Transitions</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="patent-card">
          <div class="patent-top">
            <span class="patent-number">08</span>
            <span class="status">COMPLETE SPECIFICATION · FILED 12 OCT 2026</span>
          </div>

          <h3>Reduced Spatial Representation Maintenance</h3>

          <p class="filed-title">
            Filed title: Method and Receiver for Bounded Maintenance of a
            Reduced Spatial Channel Representation
          </p>

          <p>
            Investigates bounded maintenance of a reduced spatial channel
            representation as receiver conditions change.
          </p>

          <div class="meta">
            <span>RESEARCH AREA</span>
            <strong>Spatial Processing / Receiver State</strong>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-pattern">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="section-label">PORTFOLIO PATTERN</p>

      <h2>One research program, multiple receiver problems.</h2>

      <div class="chain">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Acquire</strong>
          <p>Acquire only the channel information that is useful.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Estimate</strong>
          <p>Track channel evolution as propagation conditions change.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Represent</strong>
          <p>Exploit channel structure rather than assuming arbitrary coupling.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Equalize</strong>
          <p>Adapt receiver processing to observed interference conditions.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <strong>Detect</strong>
          <p>Adapt processing support to the structure present in the signal.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="status-section">
    <div class="container two-column">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">PORTFOLIO STATUS</p>
        <h2>Filed and continuing to develop.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="status-grid">
        <div>
          <strong>2026</strong>
          <span>Initial filing year</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>4</strong>
          <span>Provisional applications</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>4</strong>
          <span>Complete specifications</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <strong>In progress</strong>
          <span>Portfolio development</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="research-link">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="section-label">IP EMERGES FROM RESEARCH</p>

      <h2>The filings are part of a broader engineering program.</h2>

      <p>
        The portfolio emerges from ongoing work across wireless signal
        processing, channel structure, mobility and Doppler, adaptive
        estimation and tracking, equalization, signal detection and
        physics-accurate simulation.
      </p>

      <div class="links">
        <a href="/research/">Explore research →</a>
        <a href="/artifacts/">Explore engineering artifacts →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .ip-hero {
    padding: 112px 0 96px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label,
  .patent-number,
  .status,
  .meta span,
  .chain span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 20px 0 26px;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .ip-boundary,
  .portfolio-section,
  .portfolio-pattern,
  .status-section,
  .research-link {
    padding: 112px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .two-column {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: 80px;
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 14px 0 28px;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 700px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .portfolio {
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .patent-card {
    min-height: 370px;
    padding: 34px;
    background: var(--surface);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .patent-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 54px;
  }

  .patent-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .filed-title {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .patent-card > p:not(.filed-title) {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 600px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .meta {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 30px;
  }

  .meta span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .meta strong {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  .portfolio-pattern {
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .chain {
    margin-top: 48px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .chain > div {
    min-height: 190px;
    padding: 26px;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .chain span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 38px;
  }

  .chain strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .chain p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .status-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .status-grid div {
    min-height: 140px;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .status-grid strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .status-grid span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .research-link {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .research-link > .narrow > p:not(.section-label) {
    max-width: 720px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 18px 30px;
    margin-top: 28px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1050px) {
    .chain {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .two-column {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 36px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .ip-hero {
      padding: 82px 0 74px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 10vw, 3.2rem);
    }

    .ip-boundary,
    .portfolio-section,
    .portfolio-pattern,
    .status-section,
    .research-link {
      padding: 78px 0;
    }

    .portfolio,
    .chain,
    .status-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .patent-card {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .patent-top {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 34px;
    }

    .status {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    .chain > div {
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
